  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A box contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of liquid water in equilibrium&nbsp;with water vapour at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The equilibrium vapour pressure of water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;Torr. When the volume of the box is increased, some of the liquid water evaporates to maintain the equilibrium pressure. If all the liquid water evaporates, then the volume of the box must be ______ litre. [nearest integer]</p><p>(Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>082</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>_</p><p>(Ignore the volume of the liquid water and assume water vapours behave as an ideal gas.)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "29",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Applying ideal gas equation,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PV</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>nRT</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>where</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pressure</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>volume</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>moles</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Universal</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gas</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>constant</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Temperature</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>nRT</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>82</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>760</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>21</mn></math>Litres</p><p>Hence, the volume of the box is 29 litres(In integer)</p>"
  }
}